1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,586
This tutorial covers the everyday work on

2
00:00:02,586 --> 00:00:05,172
a tenancy contract once it is active.

3
00:00:05,172 --> 00:00:08,127
As a Company Admin, open the contract for

4
00:00:08,127 --> 00:00:10,713
unit M-1501, posted in the previous
tutorial.

5
00:00:10,713 --> 00:00:12,191
Its status is Active.

6
00:00:12,191 --> 00:00:15,515
Record payment and Renew sit at the top,
and

7
00:00:15,515 --> 00:00:18,840
More actions holds the rest: extend,
amend, add a

8
00:00:18,840 --> 00:00:22,165
charge, transfer, give notice, terminate,
and the tenant's ledger.

9
00:00:22,165 --> 00:00:24,751
A posted contract is never edited
directly;

10
00:00:24,751 --> 00:00:26,967
each change is its own entry.

11
00:00:26,967 --> 00:00:29,923
Sara is taking a second parking bay from

12
00:00:29,923 --> 00:00:32,878
the first of October, so select Add
charge.

13
00:00:32,878 --> 00:00:35,833
Set the effective date, enter the Ejari
number

14
00:00:35,833 --> 00:00:38,419
of the addendum, and give a reason.

15
00:00:38,419 --> 00:00:41,375
Add a Parking Fee line of 750, which

16
00:00:41,375 --> 00:00:44,330
is earned over the rest of the term.

17
00:00:44,330 --> 00:00:48,393
Then enter the cheque that pays for it,
number 500406, for

18
00:00:48,393 --> 00:00:52,088
the same amount, and the cheques match the
addendum's value.

19
00:00:52,088 --> 00:00:53,196
Select Add charge.

20
00:00:53,196 --> 00:00:57,629
The contract value rises to 140,750, and
there are now six cheques.

21
00:00:57,629 --> 00:00:59,106
Open the Attachments tab.

22
00:00:59,106 --> 00:01:02,062
Under Addenda and Ejari, the addendum is
listed

23
00:01:02,062 --> 00:01:05,017
with its own journal and its Ejari number.

24
00:01:05,017 --> 00:01:07,972
Supporting documents keep the paperwork
with the contract.

25
00:01:07,972 --> 00:01:11,667
Type a name, Move-in inspection report,
and attach the file.

26
00:01:11,667 --> 00:01:15,361
It is listed with buttons to download or
delete it.

27
00:01:15,361 --> 00:01:18,316
Open the Activities tab and select Log
interaction.

28
00:01:18,316 --> 00:01:21,641
Choose Call and Outbound, and write a
short summary.

29
00:01:21,641 --> 00:01:24,227
Set the outcome to Positive, and save.

30
00:01:24,227 --> 00:01:27,921
The note records who logged it and when,
so whoever

31
00:01:27,921 --> 00:01:31,615
picks up the contract next can see what
was agreed.

32
00:01:31,615 --> 00:01:36,048
Keep notes factual, and never put
passwords or card details in them.
